/-!
# Model and generation for the plus-four branch

The original star map identifies U* with the singular-point stabilizer E₄.
The two nonorthogonal marked points give starred generation, which lifts
through the normalizing two-core and O²(L)=L to I=LU. The module is
I-irreducible and central in O₂(I), S≤T normalizes U, and the intrinsic
quotient comparisons preserve the original projection and natural action.
They use the actual orthogonal and ordered symmetric-group carriers, with
the original L-image identified with A₃×A₃.

The marked hyperplanes span V_L and intersect in E₄; the displacement
calculation proves V_L∩U=V and its conjugate. The singularity, stabilizer
and generation premises of the earlier helpers are discharged here.
Applying the independent central-kernel theorem gives S=WWᵍ with its
model and normalization premises discharged. The quotient-module
decomposition remains with the full G.2.6 assembly.
Source: Aschbacher–Smith, G.2.6, printed p.336, and G.2.3(2), p.333.
-/
